      "ayah_id": "21:65",
      "ayah_arabic": "ثُمَّ نُكِسُواْ عَلَىٰ رُءُوسِهِمۡ لَقَدۡ عَلِمۡتَ مَا هَٰٓؤُلَآءِ يَنطِقُونَ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "Al-Anbiyaa",
      "literal_gloss": "they were turned",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "Then they reversed themselves, [saying], \"You have already known that these do not speak!\"",
        "pickthall": "And they were utterly confounded, and they said: Well thou knowest that these speak not.",
        "khattab": "Then they ˹quickly˺ regressed to their ˹original˺ mind-set, ˹arguing,˺ “You already know that those ˹idols˺ cannot talk.”",
        "arberry": "Then they were utterly put to confusion saying, 'Very well indeed thou knowest these do not speak.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
        32,
        12,
        5
      ],
      "form_arabic": "نَاكِسُوا@",
      "lemma": "naAkisuwA",
      "lemma_arabic": "نَاكِسُوا",
      "pos": "N",
      "ayah_id": "32:12",
      "ayah_arabic": "وَلَوۡ تَرَىٰٓ إِذِ ٱلۡمُجۡرِمُونَ نَاكِسُواْ رُءُوسِهِمۡ عِندَ رَبِّهِمۡ رَبَّنَآ أَبۡصَرۡنَا وَسَمِعۡنَا فَٱرۡجِعۡنَا نَعۡمَلۡ صَٰلِحًا إِنَّا مُوقِنُونَ",
      "surah_revelation": "Meccan",
      "surah_name": "As-Sajda",
      "literal_gloss": "(will) hang",
      "translations": {
        "saheeh": "If you could but see when the criminals are hanging their heads before their Lord, [saying], \"Our Lord, we have seen and heard, so return us [to the world]; we will work righteousness. Indeed, we are [now] certain.\"",
        "pickthall": "Couldst thou but see when the guilty hang their heads before their Lord, (and say): Our Lord! We have now seen and heard, so send us back; we will do right, now we are sure.",
        "khattab": "If only you could see the wicked hanging their heads ˹in shame˺ before their Lord, ˹crying:˺ “Our Lord! We have now seen and heard, so send us back and we will do good. We truly have sure faith ˹now˺!”",
        "arberry": "Ah, if thou couldst see the guilty hanging their heads before their Lord! 'Our Lord, we have seen and heard; now return us, that we may do righteousness, for we have sure faith.'"
      }
    },
    {
      "location": [
